# Decision Point Framework

Spec: DecisionPoint

Purpose:
  Defines the structure and behavior of post-execution decision
  points. After every major task or /sdd* command completion,
  a structured summary is emitted containing recommended next
  steps, risk assessment, and workflow control options.

Owns: workflow\decision-point.sdd

Why:
  Without structured decision points, users face unbounded
  next-step choices and no clear mechanism to pause for review.
  Decision points make the workflow controlled, informative,
  and auditable.

DecisionPointSchema:
  id: DP-{timestamp}-{random}
  type: CONTINUE | GATE | DECISION | ERROR | REVIEW
  triggeredBy: command or task that produced this
  stage: current chain stage (BE, FE, MD, VR, etc.)
  result: outcome summary (PASS, BLOCK, WARN, COMPLETE, etc.)
  recommendedNextSteps:
    - id: step identifier
      label: short action label
      command: command to execute
      description: what this entails
      risk: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
  reviewOptions:
    approveAndProceed: command to auto-advance
    reviewAndModify: command to enter review mode
  metadata:
    timestamp: ISO-8601
    sessionId: session correlation ID
    taskId: linked TASK ID (optional)
    decisionId: linked DEC ID (optional)
    evidence: supporting references (optional)

DecisionTypeSemantics:
  CONTINUE:
    description: Proceed to next recommended step (default)
    auto_approve: safe for non-gate results
  GATE:
    description: Human gate requires approval before proceeding
    auto_approve: requires --approve flag or human confirmation
  DECISION:
    description: Fork — user must choose between paths
    auto_approve: never auto-advances; requires explicit choice
  ERROR:
    description: Blocked by error; fix required before proceeding
    auto_approve: never auto-advances; requires fix
  REVIEW:
    description: Needs review/modification before proceeding
    auto_approve: requires --review flag to enter review mode

EmissionTriggers:
  after_command:
    event: Every /sdd* command completion
    location: CommandRunner.run() before return
    fields: command result mapped to DecisionPoint
  after_gate:
    event: Gate decision (security, human, verification)
    location: Gate runtime, HookBridge
    fields: gate result + available next steps
  after_stage:
    event: Chain stage transition (BE→FE→MD→VR)
    location: execution-runner.ts
    fields: stage result + parallel branch status
  after_task:
    event: Task completion (DONE proof)
    location: execution-loop.sdd Step 15
    fields: task result + knowledge gate status

EmissionProtocol:
  step_1: Determine decision type from result
  step_2: Build recommendedNextSteps (1-5 steps, ranked by priority)
  step_3: Define reviewOptions based on decision type
  step_4: Persist JSON to .sdd/runtime/decisions/{id}.json
  step_5: Emit OBS event (OBS17 for CONTINUE, OBS18 for GATE, OBS19 for REVIEW, OBS20 for ERROR)
  step_6: Output human-readable summary to command output

Persistence:
  location: .sdd/runtime/decisions/{DP-id}.json
  format: JSON (DecisionPoint schema)
  retention: permanent (audit trail)
  index: .sdd/runtime/decisions/INDEX.sdd (append-only)

Rules:
  [DP-01] Every /sdd* command MUST emit a Decision Point after execution.
  [DP-02] Decision Points MUST NOT block command execution — they are emitted after the fact.
  [DP-03] recommendedNextSteps MUST be actionable (valid command strings).
  [DP-04] GATE and DECISION types MUST NOT auto-approve without explicit flag.
  [DP-05] Every Decision Point MUST be persisted as JSON for audit.
  [DP-06] OBS events (OBS17-OBS20) MUST include DecisionPoint id.
  [DP-07] Decision Points MUST include risk level for every recommended step.
  [DP-08] reviewAndModify MUST accept the user back into the workflow at current stage.
  [DP-09] Empty next steps (no valid continuation) → type ERROR.
  [DP-10] --approve flag on /sdd-next auto-advances from CONTINUE/REVIEW types.

OBS Mapping:
  OBS17: decision_point_emitted — CONTINUE type
  OBS18: decision_point_gate — GATE type
  OBS19: decision_point_review — REVIEW type
  OBS20: decision_point_error — ERROR type

WorkflowControl:
  approve_and_proceed:
    command: /sdd-next --approve
    behavior: Auto-advances from CONTINUE or REVIEW types; pauses at GATE/DECISION/ERROR
  review_and_modify:
    command: /sdd-next --review
    behavior: Re-opens current stage for modification; all context preserved

State: +
